msgstr "Gunakan `catalog.backends()` untuk melihat senarai backend yang tersedia daripada akaun/instans pengguna.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If no backend is specified, the least-busy backend (the one with the least number of pending jobs) is automatically selected.\n"
msgstr "Jika tiada backend dinyatakan, backend yang paling kurang sibuk (iaitu yang mempunyai bilangan kerja tertangguh yang paling sedikit) dipilih secara automatik.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Once the optimizer is loaded (see previous), you can run it on the problem using default options:\n"
msgstr "Setelah pengoptimum dimuatkan (lihat sebelumnya), anda boleh menjalankannya pada masalah menggunakan pilihan lalai:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Check the job status as follows:\n"
msgstr "Semak status kerja seperti berikut:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Retrieve results as follows:\n"
msgstr "Dapatkan hasil seperti berikut:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Printing the results gives the following:\n"
msgstr "Mencetak hasil memberikan yang berikut:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The `solution` dictionary corresponds to the qubits defined in the problem ($s_0, s_1$, and $s_2$) and gives their optimized spin values.\n"
msgstr "Kamus `solution` sepadan dengan qubit yang ditakrifkan dalam masalah ($s_0, s_1$, dan $s_2$) dan memberikan nilai spin yang dioptimumkan bagi setiap satu.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The `objective_value` is the cost or energy of the optimization problem. It quantifies the `solution` quality.\n"
msgstr "`objective_value` ialah kos atau tenaga bagi masalah pengoptimuman. Ia mengukur kualiti `solution`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`metadata` gives information on the transpilation (two-qubit gate counts/depth, gates used, active qubits) and various runtimes for both quantum and classical compute time.\n"
msgstr "`metadata` memberikan maklumat mengenai transpilasi (bilangan/kedalaman get dua-qubit, get yang digunakan, qubit aktif) dan pelbagai masa jalan untuk kedua-dua masa pengkomputeran kuantum dan klasik.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Additionally, `metadata` provides a glimpse into the internal workings of the algorithm. You can see the optimized variational parameters (beta and gamma) and review how the distribution of measured bitstrings improved after classical post-processing was applied to the raw quantum results.\n"
msgstr "Selain itu, `metadata` memberikan gambaran ke dalam cara kerja dalaman algoritma. Anda boleh melihat parameter variasi yang dioptimumkan (beta dan gamma) dan menyemak bagaimana taburan rentetan bit (bitstring) yang diukur bertambah baik selepas pasca-pemprosesan klasik diterapkan pada hasil kuantum mentah.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"All bitstrings in the result output can be mapped to the problem variables by using the `variable_mapping`.\n"
"For example, you can map the `'solution_bitstring': '100'` with the `'variable_mapping': {'0': 0, '1': 1, '2': 2}` to the binary solution: `{'0': 1, '1': 0, '2': 0}`.\n"
"Since you are solving the problem in terms of spin variables, you need to apply the binary to spin transformation  (`0` -> `1`, `1` -> `-1` ).\n"
"You then arrive at the final solution `'solution': {'0': -1, '1': 1, '2': 1}`.\n"
msgstr ""
"Semua rentetan bit dalam output hasil boleh dipetakan kepada pemboleh ubah masalah dengan menggunakan `variable_mapping`.\n"
"Sebagai contoh, anda boleh memetakan `'solution_bitstring': '100'` dengan `'variable_mapping': {'0': 0, '1': 1, '2': 2}` kepada penyelesaian binari: `{'0': 1, '1': 0, '2': 0}`.\n"
"Memandangkan anda menyelesaikan masalah dari segi pemboleh ubah spin, anda perlu menerapkan transformasi binari kepada spin (`0` -> `1`, `1` -> `-1` ).\n"
"Anda kemudian akan sampai kepada penyelesaian akhir `'solution': {'0': -1, '1': 1, '2': 1}`.\n"

